# Challenge70 (NewScenario22 topology) — VMware Vagrantfile
#
# NOTE: router-1 has r2r degree 4 (6 total adapters: NAT + mgmt + 4 r2r
# links). Per the documented lesson from Challenge101/Challenge130/Challenge78,
# expect the PCI-bridge slot overflow / vnet misbinding on router-1 the first
# time this box is brought up fresh — budget time for the manual GUI
# vnet-reassignment fix (or check whether this box's .vmx wiring is already
# correct despite the guest-naming scramble, per the Challenge78 instance) if
# router-1 is unreachable via plain ssh even though `vagrant ssh router-1`
# and `ip -br a` inside the guest both look correct.
#
# :networks order on each router MUST match that router's r2r_interfaces key
# order in ../../data/config.json — both are hand-maintained, nothing
# derives one from the other automatically.

